},{"text":"IncidenceList","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"IncidenceList","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","title":"IncidenceList","identifier":"doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceList","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A directed hypergraph stored as an incidence list: each hyperedge’s sources and targets, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"each vertex’s out- and in-hyperedges (its forward and backward stars), as two planes of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UndirectedIncidenceList"},{"type":"text","text":"’s storage."}],"url":"\/documentation\/hypergraphs\/incidencelist"},"doc://Hypergraphs/documentation/Hypergraphs/IncidenceGraphView":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An undirected hypergraph’s incidence graph, read lazily from its storage: a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Graph"},{"type":"text","text":" on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0 ..< n + m"},{"type":"text","text":" whose vertex "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"i < n"},{"type":"text","text":" is the hypergraph’s vertex index "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"i"},{"type":"text","text":" and whose vertex "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"n + p"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is hyperedge "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"p"},{"type":"text","text":", with an edge "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"{i, n + p}"},{"type":"text","text":" for each incidence. It is bipartite and simple"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(vertices on the left, hyperedges on the right), an empty hyperedge is an isolated vertex, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it loses nothing."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"IncidenceGraphView","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/hypergraphs\/incidencegraphview","title":"IncidenceGraph